builtin tool implementation plans
=================================

one file per builtin tool from the spec's phase 2 (sections "mcp tools
(new, structured)" and following). since 2026-07-11 the directory also
holds phase-3 plans, which may cover a feature or a tool family
rather than a single tool: mcp_tool_registry (the registry pivot),
tool_scope (the tool_scope_* builtin family), mcp_tool_command (the
mcp_tool/mcp_resource outer syntax + params machinery),
builtin_activation (scala builtins mirrored into the ML registry so
one activation layer governs both kinds, decided 2026-07-13). each plan pins down, for one tool:

- advertised metadata: exposed name, description text, inputSchema
  (json property names = the yxml pair keys of the argument encoding),
  annotations. this is the exact data for the scala builtin table row.
- backing mechanism and the name/argument mapping across the layers
  (mcp name -> bridge fname -> engine function).
- implementation steps, smallest first, each independently verifiable.
- ASSUMPTIONS the tool relies on — infrastructure it presumes, prover
  behavior it presumes, spec decisions it depends on — each with the
  concrete test that checks it, placed in the four-layer pyramid
  (ml unit / scala unit / bridge / e2e; see the spec's "testing
  architecture" and phase 2 "testing" sections).

testing process (since 2026-07-10, munit migration -- see CHANGELOG
"testing infrastructure"): the pyramid's layer names are unchanged,
but the scala layers are now munit suites in the separate mcp_test/
component. new [scala unit] cases go in a suite in
mcp_test/src/mcp_handler_tests.scala over Fake_Backend (which lives
in mcp_test/src/mcp_testing.scala); new [bridge] cases in
mcp_test/src/mcp_bridge_tests.scala, extending MCP_Session_Suite
(one headless PIDE session per suite; with_repl / slow_step /
await_busy / eventually / expect_ok / expect_error fixtures);
register new suites in mcp_test/src/mcp_test_tool.scala. run:
isabelle mcp_test [-b] [-t PATTERN]. plans written before the
migration say things like "scala unit round-trips in isabelle
mcp_test" -- read those through this mapping.

added 2026-07-10: MCP_Heap_Suite (mcp_test/src/mcp_testing.scala), a
third fixture between [scala unit] and [bridge] -- raw ML evaluated
by a fresh `isabelle ML_process` against a saved heap (ml / ml_check
/ ml_test helpers; suites go in mcp_test/src/mcp_heap_tests.scala,
run under -b). use it for FRESH-PROCESS/heap-restart claims, the one
environment neither build-time \<^assert> theories (they run inside
the building process, where e.g. Thy_Info segments still exist) nor
Fake_Backend can exercise: Thy_Info keying, name-space entry
survival, whether recorded segments reach a fresh process (they do,
for record_theories heaps -- the old "segments KNOWN GAP" was
retracted 2026-07-10, see CHANGELOG; it was the name-normalization
bug in disguise), and the like (see plans/find_definition's entities
notes). it has NO Scala context -- \<^scala>, protocol commands and
PIDE snapshots still need MCP_Session_Suite. heap loads cost seconds:
batch related assertions into one ml() call.

plans refine the spec where per-tool honesty demands it (e.g. the
spec's coarse "repl_* is mutating" annotation blanket vs the actually
read-only repl_list); every such refinement is flagged with
"spec refinement:" so it can be folded back into the spec.

each plan has a parallel agent evaluation under evals/ (same name:
evals/repl_step for plans/repl_step). plans verify the mechanism;
evaluations verify the abstraction — given only a task, does an
agent find the tool, call it correctly, recover from its errors?
evaluation failures feed the reflection loop described in
evals/README and can send a tool back to the spec for a second
implementation.

status key: [ ] planned only, [x] implemented and green.

index (wave order from the spec's implementation plan)
------------------------------------------------------

wave 0 — shared infrastructure (prerequisites, not tools):
  MCP_Session.ir promise-by-id bridge; named-args yxml encoding on
  both sides; builtin tool table + tools/list merge + tools/call
  dispatch. assumptions owned by these are stated once in the pilot
  plan (repl_list) and referenced as I1..I5 by later plans.

wave 1 — repl lifecycle + stepping + proof search (MCP.ir bridge):
  - [x] repl_list              plans/repl_list   (pilot: full template)
  - [x] repl_init              plans/repl_init
  - [ ] repl_init_from_source  plans/repl_init_from_source
  - [ ] repl_fork              plans/repl_fork
  - [x] repl_remove            plans/repl_remove
  - [x] repl_step              plans/repl_step
  - [x] repl_state             plans/repl_state
  - [x] repl_show              plans/repl_show
  - [x] repl_text              plans/repl_text
  - [x] repl_edit              plans/repl_edit
  - [x] repl_replay            plans/repl_replay
  - [x] repl_truncate          plans/repl_truncate
  - [x] repl_back              plans/repl_back
  - [x] repl_merge             plans/repl_merge
  - [x] repl_timeout           plans/repl_timeout
  - [x] repl_pin               plans/repl_pin
  - [x] repl_unpin             plans/repl_unpin
  - [x] repl_rebase            plans/repl_rebase
  - [x] sledgehammer           plans/sledgehammer
  - [x] find_theorems          plans/find_theorems

wave 2 — theory management (headless use_theories, scala side):
  - [x] load_theory            plans/load_theory
  - [x] unload_theory          plans/unload_theory
  - [x] check_theory           plans/check_theory

wave 3 — library discovery (session-structure index, scala side):
  - [x] session_structure      plans/session_structure (umbrella:
        startup structure/deps + resolve_theory infra, filesystem-tier
        resource widening, load_theory session-qualified resolution;
        the tools below build on it)
  - [x] list_sessions          plans/list_sessions
  - [x] list_theories          plans/list_theories
  - [x] search_sources         plans/search_sources

wave 4 — scope + navigation:
  - [x] scope_add              plans/scope_add
  - [x] scope_remove           plans/scope_remove
  - [x] scope_show             plans/scope_show
  - [x] find_definition        plans/find_definition   (MCP.ir, name-space lookup)
  - [ ] goto_definition        plans/goto_definition   (scala, snapshot entity markup)
  - [x] find_theorems (context promotion)  plans/find_theorems,
        "context promotion" section — repl becomes optional,
        theory accepted, default = base image (decided 2026-07-12;
        aligns the finding tools on one context interface. the
        wave-1 [x] above is the shipped repl-required version.)

wave 5 — documentation (Doc catalog + src/Doc sources, scala side;
  spec "documentation for the agent", decided 2026-07-14):
  - [x] doc_list               plans/doc_list  (Doc.contents()
        catalog joined to doc sessions via document_variants)
  - [x] doc_read               plans/doc_read  (toc + section reads
        over chapter .thy sources; plain entries windowed; depends
        on doc_list's Doc_Catalog — implement doc_list first)

flagged, NOT scheduled (no wave):
  - read_theory                plans/read_theory   (tool mirror of
        isabelle://theory/{name}, for clients without resource
        support — see spec "resource-read tool mirrors")
  - list_entities              plans/list_entities (tool mirror of
        .../entities, same rationale)
